export anchor ChartGridStyle:
    number: 210
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Chart grid
    idea: Four equal chart cards answer the week at a glance, with tasks per day, status, completion per project and hours, framed by an icon rail on the left and a running activity column on the right.
    base: light
    palette:
        mist: #eef1f4, the page and inset panels
        white: #ffffff, cards, the rail and the activity column
        ink: #1c2733, text and figures
        slate: #52606d, labels, axes and times
        line: #dde3e9, dividers and gridlines, never text
        teal: #0f766e, the primary button, this week bars, On track and the focus ring
        tealLight: #9fd8cf, last week bars, never text
        tealTint: #e3f4f1, the current rail item and a focused row
        track: #e6eaee, the empty part of bars and the gauge
        amber: #b7791f, the At risk slice, never text
        amberText: #8a5300, the At risk label
        red: #c53030, the Behind slice
        redText: #b42318, the Behind label, the overdue figure and the badge
    type:
        One stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Ubuntu, Helvetica Neue,
        Arial. The gauge figure is 34px bold, KPI figures 24px bold, the
        greeting 22px bold, card titles 15px bold, body 14px and meta and
        axis text 12px in slate.
    layout:
        A 76px white icon rail on the left holds a teal rounded square
        logo and six nav items stacked, each a 22px line icon with an 11px
        label beneath, Home on a teal tint. A 300px white activity column
        runs down the right as a vertical timeline of round initials with
        a thin connecting line. The centre starts with a row of the
        greeting Hello Mara, here is your week in charts with the date and
        a red square with 4 tasks are overdue, then a pill search, a teal
        pill New project button, a round bell with a red count badge and a
        round avatar. One white card splits into four KPI cells by thin
        dividers. Then a two by two grid of equal cards holds a column
        chart of tasks per day in light and dark teal, a status donut whose
        slices carry white circle, triangle and square marks beside a list
        of counts, horizontal bars of done against total tasks per project
        scaled by project size, and a half circle gauge of 186 hours
        against a 200 hour target tick. A full width card below lists the
        projects in a compact table with mini bars. Below 1180px the
        activity column drops under the centre. Below 860px the charts go
        to one column and the KPIs to two by two. Below 640px the rail
        becomes a fixed bottom tab bar.
    spacing: An 8px base with 20px gaps between cards and 28px page padding.
    density: Medium. Four equal chart cards carry the page, figures share one strip.
    corners: 16px cards, 12px rail items and swatches, 10px fields, pill buttons and search.
    borders: Almost none. A 1px line splits the rail, the activity column and the KPI cells.
    shadows: A soft two layer card shadow, 1px tight plus 6px 20px diffuse.
    icons:
        Rounded 1.8px line icons at 22px in the rail with labels below.
        Status shapes are a filled circle, triangle and rounded square,
        also printed in white on the donut slices.
    focus: A 2px white gap then a 2px teal ring.
    tone: Friendly and brief, such as Hello Mara, here is your week in charts.
